{"content":[{"c":["MAHALAB*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Reconstructed name of a town in Asher’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.29","r":"Josh.19.29","rawR":"Josh.19.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.29","value":"Josh.19.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 19:29"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “Mehebel”); the Hebrew text has a transposition of the last two consonants, but the town is probably the same as Ahlab and Helbah of ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.1.31","r":"Judg.1.31","rawR":"Judg.1.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.1.31","value":"Judg.1.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Judges 1:31"},". The correct name is preserved in the Assyrian annals of Sennacherib as Mahalliba; another text has Mahalab. The town is sometimes identified with Khirbet el-Mahalib, northeast of Tyre."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Ahlab_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Ahlab_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Ahlab_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Ahlab"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Mahalab","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 19:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.29","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.29","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.29"},{"anchorText":"Judges 1:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.1.31","rawQueryValue":"Judg.1.31","sourceRefExact":"Judg.1.31"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3d4aff7c82cef48bbe1244520b9b16984f06cbd88772159f723461b00bf085d4","sourceItemName":"Mahalab","sourceItemOrder":54,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Mahalab","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Mahalab*","title":"Mahalab*"